// SEVERAL holes, reached by SEPARATE proofs — the shape that exposes whether the `--draft`
// disclosure is ordered by the SOURCE or by the SCHEDULE.
//
// `holes_reached` is appended to as each proof reaches its hole, so its order is the order
// the engine happened to run those proofs in. That is not part of the output contract:
// `bpa check --chaos=N` shuffles the schedule, and before the fix this file's disclosure
// listed the four holes in a different order under most seeds. The report now sorts by
// declaration site, so the list reads `holeAlpha holeBravo holeCharlie holeDelta` whatever
// order the proofs ran in.
//
// Deliberately uses four SEPARATE theorems: one proof reaching four holes would record them
// in a single proof's walk order, which is already source-ordered and would prove nothing.
pred alpha
pred bravo
pred charlie
pred delta

hole holeAlpha: alpha
hole holeBravo: bravo
hole holeCharlie: charlie
hole holeDelta: delta

theorem usesAlpha: alpha
proof
  @conclusion |
    alpha
    [by cite holeAlpha]
qed

theorem usesBravo: bravo
proof
  @conclusion |
    bravo
    [by cite holeBravo]
qed

theorem usesCharlie: charlie
proof
  @conclusion |
    charlie
    [by cite holeCharlie]
qed

theorem usesDelta: delta
proof
  @conclusion |
    delta
    [by cite holeDelta]
qed
